      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "f56dfdb9b3541965ef50753acffa1740",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"charged-current-w-and-top-decays\">Charged-current W and top decays</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><a href=\"/\">Browse notebooks</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"/?file=hep/z_decay.py\">Z decays</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"/?file=hep/higgs_decay.py\">Higgs decays</a></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Generate eight channels from <code>Model.standard_model()</code>: charged W decays to leptons, unequal-mass quarks or massless light quarks, together with top and antitop decay. Keep the chiral vertex and complex CKM factor, sum physical final polarizations and average the initial spin. The full massive-vector spin sum includes the longitudinal polarization.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The symbolic comparisons reproduce the <a href=\"https://feyncalc.github.io/FeynCalcExamples/EW/Tree/W-ElAnel\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">leptonic W</a>, <a href=\"https://feyncalc.github.io/FeynCalcExamples/EW/Tree/W-QiQjbar\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">quark W</a> and <a href=\"https://feyncalc.github.io/FeynCalcExamples/EW/Tree/Qt-QbW\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">top</a> references. Massive W quark channels use the model's charm/bottom fields to retain two nonzero, unequal masses. Their formula is independent of the chosen generations.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Write <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(H||)</marimo-tex> for the parent mass, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(x,y||)</marimo-tex> for the daughter masses and <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(V=V_R+iV_I||)</marimo-tex>. All widths use the shared two-body phase-space and decay-flux methods, with <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(e^2=4\\sqrt2 G_Fm_W^2\\sin^2\\theta_W||)</marimo-tex>. The physical domain is <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(H&gt;x+y||)</marimo-tex>; the numerical checks also include the threshold limit.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
